            "selectCount": 1,
            "bodyHtml": "<div><p>The Mangrove Regeneration Project</p><p><strong>Background:</strong></p><p><strong>Mangrove forests:</strong></p><ul><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; protect coastal areas from {{31}} by the sea</li><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; are an important habitat for wildlife</li></ul><p><strong>Problems:</strong></p><ul><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; mangroves had been used by farmers as {{32}}</li><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; mangroves were poisoned by the use of {{33}}</li><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; local people used the mangroves as a place to put their {{34}}</li></ul><p><strong>Actions taken to protect the mangroves:</strong></p><ul><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; a barrier which was made of {{35}} was constructed - but it failed</li><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; new mangroves had to be grown from seed</li><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; the seeds of the {{36}} mangrove were used</li></ul><p><strong>First set of seedlings:</strong></p><ul><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; kept in small pots in a {{37}}</li><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; Watered with {{38}} water</li><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; planted out on south side of a small island</li><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; at risk from the large {{39}} population</li></ul><p><strong>Second set of seedlings:</strong></p><ul><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; planted in the seabed near established mangrove roots</li><li>•&nbsp;&nbsp; the young plants were destroyed in a {{40}}</li></ul><p><strong>Results:</strong> The first set of seedlings was successful</p></div>",
